WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.430
"Marin (Sparkle Mode)"

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:03.400
Ta-da!

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.900
Wow, it's a Marin (Sparkling Mode)!
Those are super rare!

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:07.870
That's so nice!

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:10.510
Wow, awesome! That's so nice.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.340
Isn't it, though?

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.540
Hey, hey, look!

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.580
It is nice that kids can be so innocent.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.450
Tinoa, you look, too!

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.180
I don't care about that stuff.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.350
Oh...

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.350
Mika, look! I got a Marin (Sparkling Mode)!

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.030
A school festival performance?

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:38.100
Yes, indeedy! At Hayato's university.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.870
They're letting us do it there.
The Verbalism Club reading theater.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.710
That's at Seisou University, then?

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:49.040
The debating contest at their school festival is famous, isn't it?

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.880
Why are none of the boys here?

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.080
Hayato!

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:57.050
Akira and the boys don't seem to be here today.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.050
If you're looking for Akira or Hayato Kujyo,

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:02.420
Tsutomu Domon took them to something called a "group blind date."

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.790
B-Blind date?!

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.620
No way!

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.930
Um...!

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.900
They ran away. Victory is ours.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.810
We lost! We struck out completely!

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.310
Ah, screw it!

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:23.610
The pre-Christmas period in November was my chance to find a girlfriend!

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.080
How dull.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.450
I wondered what it was, since you dragged me here.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:33.250
And Hayato, are you aware you're the one who made things all awkward?

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.430
Isn't it cute?

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:41.000
No, I have no idea why you would decorate your fingers with cooked eels.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.930
That's way too straight a response!

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.830
I only said what I thought.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.600
And I'm telling you that's no good.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.270
You should compliment them, even if it's a lie.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.940
"They're nicely fried!" or something.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:56.140
Lie? I couldn't do that.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:58.000
"Lie"

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:06.550
<i>The world is engulfed by an unvoiced scream</i>

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:12.490
<i>and I wait for it to reach and stir</i> <i>a certain someone's heart</i>

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:18.300
<i>With strength flowing to the edges of our souls</i>

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:24.570
<i>we set out into the white</i> <i>morning haze, without hesitation</i>

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.510
<i>I want to know everything about you</i>

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:37.510
<i>But just when I thought</i>
<i>I had you, you were gone</i>

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.590
<i>It's love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:53.200
<i>These tightly-sealed, silent lips</i>

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.570
<i>gently reply back in kind</i>

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:01.840
<i>And with love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:08.350
<i>Now, from the last of the words I couldn't find,</i>

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:17.050
<i>the music begins</i>

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:32.710
"Howl! An Honest Beaten Dog"

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.580
"My Storm"

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.410
And so that's why you should make my daughter Karan

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.710
a mascot for My Storm!

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:43.120
We get a lot of offers like yours.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:47.090
You know, I'd say it depends on how much Karan wants to do it.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.890
I really want to do it!

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:51.890
Really?

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:54.230
I was lying, obviously!

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.230
I don't want to do it!

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:58.630
Karan, mind your manners.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:02.070
I don't like that guy. The way he looks at me is perverted.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.970
This weekend you have a performance with the Verbalism Club.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.740
You know, at Seisou University's school festival.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.080
That sounds nice!

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:12.450
Go and make an impression on the future elites.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:13.940
Fine...

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.120
A friend of yours?

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.920
We're in the same class, but we've never talked much.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:31.670
There's so little, we could say we emptied it and no one would be the wiser.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.290
You're right.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:47.610
Tinoa!

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:50.490
What?

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.690
Are you free this weekend?

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:55.690
Would you come to Seisou University's school festival with me?

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.960
I'm doing reading theater there!

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.630
I'm hoping you'll come see, Tinoa!

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.460
Why?

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.670
I wonder why.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:09.470
I think I might like you, Tinoa.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:10.670
That's all.

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:13.140
Karan, let's go!

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:15.470
Yeah, just a moment!

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:18.150
Here, contact me.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:19.180
Uh, but...

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:20.910
See you on Sunday!

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:26.390
I... don't have a cellphone...

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.650
"Karan Uminagi"

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.660
"Takoyaki" "Yakitori"

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.490
"Shirobaco Verbalism Club

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.490
Away Performance

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.490
Reading Theater

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.490
Straw Wars Episode 5: The Shake Rushes Back"

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:33.490
That's a lie.

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:36.160
You say you're my father?

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:38.330
But you're a woman!

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:40.070
I had a sex change!

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:41.670
I can't believe it.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.740
I'm so shocked by that!

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.680
I can't even process that my dad was the head of the Empire!

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.010
Hold it!

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:53.510
Akira, you're playing a peasant.
You can't stand out.

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:56.180
Now, Straw Flash!

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.520
Tinoa...

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.520
Delicious!

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:07.200
Who knew that eating a Shirobaco lunch box in nature was so good?

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.400
This must be what they call a picnic.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.370
She's cute, but...

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:14.200
It's a shame she's like that.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:18.570
Um, have you seen a girl?

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:19.540
What kind?

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:21.880
She has bright colored twintails,

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:24.910
she's short and has big eyes...

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.710
Twintails...

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:32.550
I don't know a monster like that.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:35.260
You don't?

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.060
"Reception

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.060
Calligraphy Association

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.060
Outdoor Caligraphy"

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:38.060
It's starting soon. The debate contest.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.060
"Savior"

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:39.550
Let's hurry!

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.560
"Seisou University

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.560
Shuho Festival

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.560
Debate Contest"

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:46.130
Hey, do you know Kujyo from the
School of Politics and Economics?

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.640
Whoa, what a hottie.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.940
And he got the top score on the entrance exam! Isn't he awesome?

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.910
Do you think he has a girlfriend?

00:06:53.910 --> 00:07:00.250
We will now begin the Seisou University
Shuho Festival Debate Contest.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:04.990
This contest will take the format of an elimination tournament.

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:08.660
In addition to a prize for the winner,

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:15.330
there will be an exhibition debate with special guest Masatsugu Kobayakawa.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:14.700
"Masatsugu Kobayakawa

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:14.700
The rising star!

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:14.700
Building a new era"

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.820
Kobayakawa?

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:21.340
Now then, let's get the debates started.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:23.270
Participants, please step forward.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:27.510
Why is he here?!

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:31.950
Jumping in without any preparation, it's Akira Kaibuki.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:35.520
His theme is: "On the merits of a savior."

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:36.950
"Theme

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:36.950
'On the merits of a savior'"

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:39.550
There is no need for debate. For I am...

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:44.490
...the savior!

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:45.990
Please make an argument.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:47.800
What?

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.460
That guy...

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.800
"Akira Kaibuki"

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.640
Want some?

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:57.640
I don't want any...

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:58.840
Eat some!

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:00.900
--I'm fine.
--I said eat!

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:05.810
Go for it, Big Brother!

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:08.350
Hayato!

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:14.550
"Theme

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:14.550
'Economic Measures'"

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:11.390
As people living in this country,

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:14.320
we must each think of ways to improve the economy.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:20.730
If we divide the national debt by the number of citizens...

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:23.830
Now, look at these estimated
GDP figures from before the war

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:28.040
and after the war into the present day.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:31.870
These are the economic measures I propose.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.840
Now, Mr. Yuuto Horishima.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:38.440
If you have questions or a proposal, go ahead.

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:43.020
This is the most effective policy to improve the economy:

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:47.390
In short, reducing the consumption tax to 0%!

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:49.520
Isn't that entirely too simplistic?

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.030
Why?

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:54.030
If you lower prices, people will be happy to buy more.

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:56.260
That's why we make it 0%!

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.260
Let's 0%!

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:07.540
Horishima's doing something silly again!

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:10.210
Seriously? Want to go check it out for a laugh?

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:14.550
Our school's debate contest has changed.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:18.090
Now it's just a rambling popularity contest.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:22.220
That sort of thing is probably more popular with the younger generation.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:23.210
"Hayato Kujyo" "Yuuto Horishima"

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:28.800
I see. So the others already went back to Shirobaco.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:32.570
I think you were right, Big Brother.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:35.400
What was with your opponent?
He was so vapid.

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.410
But he captivated the audience.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.840
What they were looking for wasn't someone who was right.

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:47.520
My father, the senator, was terrible at speeches.

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:52.590
Because lying was against his nature, he couldn't exaggerate.

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:55.090
They weren't entertaining in the least.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:57.760
"His speeches could cure insomnia."

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:01.330
They often said things like that behind his back.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:05.770
I looked down on my father for that.
Until something happened.

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:07.130
What happened?

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:09.500
It's a boring story.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:14.680
When I was in middle school, cheating on tests was rampant among my friends.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:20.650
No one felt any guilt about showing their test papers to one another.

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:23.990
But I couldn't follow that trend.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:27.960
I couldn't lie to the teacher.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:32.530
Because of my report, a number of them were suspended.

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:35.800
However, that made life hard for me.

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:40.370
Ultimately, I transferred out before they came back from suspension.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:43.870
But... you didn't do anything bad.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:45.470
No.

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:50.180
To them, my righteousness was wrong.

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:53.650
But I couldn't choose any other path.

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:57.490
At this rate, my dream of becoming a politician to change Japan

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:59.890
is likely to end as just a dream.

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:02.320
That's not true...

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.830
The words are in pain...

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:08.060
Culture must be the accumulation of people's karma.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:13.370
That's all the more reason you must free them, no?

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:22.440
Rejoice. I shall now set you free.

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:31.250
A M.J.B.K. has appeared?

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.190
Ah, but...

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:35.250
I don't see anything happening, do you?

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.770
You're pushing it too hard.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:53.210
Even if you can handle the strain, your machine is going to break down.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:57.040
It only needs to hold out a little longer.
When can you have it fixed by?

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:59.410
I want two weeks.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:00.880
Okay.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:02.950
Isn't it possible that the M.J.B.K.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:07.390
that's on a rampage right now will defeat your enemy for you?

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:09.320
If it happens, it happens.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:15.900
Sousei Gattai. Shout.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:19.730
Aquarion!

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:34.610
San!

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:40.290
Akira seems to be using
Vector-Ga without any problems.

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.420
For now, yes.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:44.660
The word corrosion rate is rising!

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.150
But this is...

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:57.100
"Proposal

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:57.100
New Commercial Idea

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:57.100
'Use a Famous Actor'

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:57.100
That is all"

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:52.100
What do you think? It's a novel idea, isn't it?

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:53.970
It's so cutting edge!

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:57.260
I've never seen an idea so unique before!

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:00.510
Well?

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:02.940
That style is so you! You're adorable!

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:04.780
You could be a model!

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.950
C-Can I become a pro?

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:09.980
You can! I'm sure of it!

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:12.950
Don't you think it's actually gotten <i>more</i> peaceful?

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:19.460
The proliferation of white lies has eliminated conflict between people.

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:22.330
Could this actually be a good thing?

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:24.960
No, this is dangerous.

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.470
I sense something!

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:31.310
There?!

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.340
Did I get it?

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.670
No, it was a fake!

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:34.880
Uso!

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:38.680
Uso! Uso!

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:40.410
Uso!

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:45.690
The fog is too thick. I can't get a grasp on its real shape.

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.310
A fog of lies...

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:51.860
Akira and Maia are already fighting!

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:53.760
We'd better hurry, too!

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:57.060
"Miss Seisou University"

00:13:57.030 --> 00:14:00.230
I'm so ugly, I'm sure I'll lose.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:03.700
That's not true at all.
You're the cutest here, Yuuko!

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:05.740
No matter who wins, let's not hold it against each other.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:08.410
La! La! La! La! La! Goalie! Goalie!

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:11.680
What is that rhythm joke? It's hilarious!

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:13.170
You're funny.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:16.070
What is it?

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:22.020
This is kind of... creepy.

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:26.960
"Shoko Iwagami"

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:27.230
We've got a problem!
It's the word corrosion rate!

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:31.700
It's rising rapidly, with your university at the center of it!

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:34.200
An economic downturn with no end in sight,

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:37.710
and a rise in the number of temporary employees.

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:47.980
"Senator Masatsugu Kobayakawa

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:47.980
Special Debate

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:47.980
'Theory of Happiness in the Modern Era'"

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:44.280
Current university students must have uncertainties about finding a job.

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:47.950
However, just looking down will never change anything.

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:52.450
It is at a time like this that we most need to join hands.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:57.220
For each of us to realize a world where we live in equality and happiness,

00:14:57.220 --> 00:15:00.230
what we most need now is bonds between us.

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:03.720
I have no retort. You are amazing,
Senator Kobayakawa.

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:04.770
"Anomalous M.J.B.K. Value Activation"

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:07.300
Videos of the senator making his speech are spreading,

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:10.570
and that seems to be causing the rise in the word corrosion rate.

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:12.740
It just won't stop.

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:16.080
I know him! He's a politician by the name of Kobayakawa.

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:18.580
He's famous as the young hope of the ruling party.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:22.120
Why would his speech raise the word corrosion rate?

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.650
Everyone is uncertain.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.490
Big Brother Hayato?

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:28.960
Having an opinion is difficult.

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:31.930
Because it can be rejected by others.

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:37.970
Thinking is hard, too.
Because there may be no answers.

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:39.770
If you don't want to be hurt,

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:43.270
you can live surrounded by pleasant-sounding lies.

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:48.780
Giving yourself up to a big lie must be a simple and happy way to live.

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:50.110
Big Brother...

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.950
Yes, I know.

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:54.950
That's the life the majority of citizens choose.

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.450
If people want to be caught up in the flow,

00:15:57.450 --> 00:16:01.460
the proper path for a politician is to lead them that way.

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:03.690
However, even still, I...

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:06.020
What's your problem?

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:08.660
Tinoa?!

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:11.630
Apologize! You broke it!

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:13.700
I... I'm telling you, you're wrong!

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.140
I saw it.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:17.200
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.540
It is <i>not</i> fine!

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:23.140
Don't blame our princess!
The person who made it says it's fine!

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:24.650
What's with this kid?

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.380
Hey, we can go now, right?

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.380
Yes.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.480
It was nothing special, anyway.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:33.350
Why are you smiling?! I saw it!

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:44.160
You looked so sad.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:46.900
When you say it's fine, you're lying!

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.660
Shut up, you noisy brat!

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.210
I understand.

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:57.680
No matter what those around you say, you can't back down on some things.

00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:01.520
You're so awkward, you can only live honestly.

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:05.420
That's right. There are kids like you out there, too.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:09.090
What can we do?

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:13.090
If we can just clear the fog of lies a little...

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.700
How?

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:18.100
We need to bring the will of the people back.

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:19.870
I will say it again and again.

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:24.570
Believe! Through that, you will find the future!

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:27.040
Senator Kobayakawa.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:29.580
Everything you're saying is a lie.

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:31.580
Lie? Me?

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:33.880
Tinoa, this way!

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:37.050
You said people are equal.

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:39.590
Then are you and I equal?

00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:41.560
Absolutely not.

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:44.890
You were born into a family that's been in politics for generations.

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:49.230
You were virtually guaranteed success from the moment you were born.

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:52.570
Athletic ability, intelligence, personality...

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:56.240
In all things, people have characteristics they were born with.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:59.740
It's something we all must have learned when we were little.

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:02.240
Every person is different.

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:04.950
And if we are, there's no way we can be equal.

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:09.920
Despite that, people delude themselves with the sweet lie of equality.

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.250
Why?

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:15.620
Because they don't want to recognize their own inferiority.

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:18.260
That's why they cling to the comfortable lie!

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:21.600
The way you think underrates people entirely too much.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:24.330
It may be true that there are differences between people,

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:27.770
but that gives all the more meaning to us walking hand in hand.

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:29.840
Those are nothing but pretty words.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:34.140
We walk hand in hand, but then what?
We form bonds, but to what end?

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:38.810
Without thinking further than that, your means have become the end.

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:41.320
There's no meaning in that existence!

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:45.650
What is truly necessary is for each of us to think.

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:49.460
Without any mind to that, you brandish the idea of connections, bonds.

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:52.130
At its base, what you are doing is abandoning thought.

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:55.630
It's an escape for people who have become living corpses.

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:58.000
Who is this guy? He pisses me off!

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.030
Lame.

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:03.670
You need to have a little more faith.
Believe in the potential of people!

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:06.310
What will belief alone change?

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:07.670
To connect with others

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:11.810
and get by in a society which approves of never going against the tide,

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:15.350
you need to lie to yourself and make yourself match others.

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:21.020
And those awkward people who can't do that are just ostracized.

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:25.530
Lies have become a necessary lubricant for society.

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:31.170
However, despite that, I cannot accept lies!

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:35.840
Living truthfully, not lying, not going with the flow, is difficult.

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:39.710
The honest are seen as fools.
That is the sad truth.

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:40.840
However!

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:46.750
There are awkward people who won't cling to lies, no matter how they suffer!

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:49.550
It is to those people I want to speak.

00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:52.550
Even knowing that the truth can never win out over lies,

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:55.260
and living in jealousy of those who are more glib,

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:59.890
there is a fool here who will still struggle against that!

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:07.190
You awkward, honest people.
Know you are not alone.

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:15.880
What's her problem? Acting like she's so great.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:18.280
Don't be such a goody two-shoes.

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:22.880
I'm not... alone...

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:25.750
Tinoa...

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:31.390
What is wrong with you?

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:35.130
The word corrosion rate has dropped slightly.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.460
The fog is clearing.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:41.070
The fog of lies spewing from its mouth had masked the truth.

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:42.560
Then...

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:50.780
I will take that from it!

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:53.780
"Lie"

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:58.420
The empty fog of lies dissipates, and with your fangs torn out,

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:55.480
"Empty"

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:59.120
"Tiger"

00:20:58.420 --> 00:21:00.820
you're no more than a paper tiger.

00:21:03.420 --> 00:21:05.190
Burst through!

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:14.990
Uso!

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.980
"Award Certificate

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.980
Special Prize

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.980
School of Politics and Economics

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.980
Second Year Student Hayato Kujyo"

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:26.610
This won't change anything.

00:21:26.610 --> 00:21:30.450
But someday, I'll fix this world

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:33.020
while still being my awkward self.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:38.160
Saying you want to do things you don't.
Saying you like things you don't, too.

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:42.800
You have to live a lie like that in show business.

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:44.160
I see.

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:49.300
I'm going to live with lies from here on. For my dream.

00:21:49.300 --> 00:21:54.470
But I think being able to live like you do is wonderful.

00:21:56.010 --> 00:22:00.510
I know now why I kept thinking about you.

00:22:00.510 --> 00:22:04.320
Hey, would you be my friend?

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:06.080
I don't want to.

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:13.180
We're heading back.

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:26.770
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:42.190
<i>With the warmth of salvation,</i>
<i>I raise my hand into the sky</i>

00:22:42.190 --> 00:22:46.930
<i>and everything in the world gains its true colors</i>

00:22:46.930 --> 00:22:49.600
<i>(Focus) A sound that was once hidden</i>

00:22:49.600 --> 00:22:52.700
<i>(on the goal) will connect us now</i>

00:22:52.700 --> 00:22:55.200
<i>Try to understand that, okay?</i>

00:22:55.200 --> 00:22:57.640
<i>So, are you ready?</i>

00:22:57.640 --> 00:23:00.440
<i>(heart and soul) These silent teardrops</i>

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:03.040
<i>(narrow escape) that flow forth now</i>

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:06.550
<i>(enamored) are proof of that person's existence</i>

00:23:06.550 --> 00:23:13.050
<i>You can't go inside your heart all alone</i>

00:23:13.050 --> 00:23:15.620
<i>I will hesitate no more</i>

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:20.790
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:23:20.790 --> 00:23:26.000
<i>A useful life, a sparkling utopia</i>

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:35.110
<i>When your heart and voice</i> <i>tremble together, you'll surpass all</i>

00:23:35.110 --> 00:23:38.510
<i>So go for your heart</i>

00:23:51.790 --> 00:23:54.800
Kokone Kikogami, I saw an extraterrestrial!

00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:57.160
It was four-legged, with a cedar tree growing out of its back!

00:23:57.160 --> 00:23:58.300
Oh, that's...

00:23:58.300 --> 00:24:01.270
Maia, that's a fairy from Suginamisaurus Island!

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:01.940
What?!

00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:04.170
Dad told me you'll have good fortune if you can catch it!

00:24:04.170 --> 00:24:05.470
We're going to catch it, Kikogami!

00:24:05.470 --> 00:24:06.840
Th-That's Namisuke...

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:08.480
Next time, Episode 19.

00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:09.710
"Episode 19: Fall in Love! Asagaya"

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:10.300
"Fall in Love! Asagaya."
